From 240811c5b24b8b2e4cd421723874b37ae8e638ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:03:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] FBar kernels: validity of the data, update and revert, thread
 counts

The data of the FBar formulation computed by kernels are marked invalid
when the gradients are computed element by element, the tangent operator
computed by kernels being then refused with an error message. The data at
the beginning of the time step are saved by `update` and restored by
`revert`: a prediction after a revert read the data of another state. The
number of threads by element is taken into account in the check of the
number of threads of the kernels adding the matrices of rank one.

Tests: two predictions separated by a revert, refusal of the tangent
operator computed by kernels from gradients computed element by element.
